{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Creation.</b> Some say it refers to the bringing into being of what did not exist, but I have already explained that the word is only from the root of וברא אתהן. Many lands have already split open and dwellers descended into them — sheol — yet its meaning is like decree." "<b>And the earth open its mouth.</b> Like ופתחה, and likewise יפצה פיהו. I have already hinted, because the soul of man on high is fashioned, it speaks of things higher than itself, after the manner of its palace, which is the body, and likewise of things lower than itself. The reason is to make the listeners understand."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The phrase 'many lands have already split open' (וכבר נבקעו מדינות רבות) is hyper-literal; Ibn Ezra appears to be citing historical or natural precedents for ground splitting open, but the construction is compressed and the referent is unclear."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:05.679124153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}